ract":"<jats:p> Knot contact homology is an ambient isotopy invariant of knots and links in [Formula: see text]. The purpose of this paper is to extend this definition to an ambient isotopy invariant of tangles and prove that gluing of tangles gives a gluing formula for knot contact homology. As a consequence of the gluing formula we obtain that the tangle contact homology detects triviality of tangles. <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1142\/s0129167x24500447","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,15]],"date-time":"2024-07-15T03:27:28Z","timestamp":1721014048000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Tangle contact homology"],"prefix":"10.1142","volume":"35","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5697-5996","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Johan","family":"Asplund","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Mathematics, Stony Brook University, 100 Nicolls Road, Stony Brook, NY 11794, United States"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"219","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,12]]},"reference":[{"key":"S0129167X24500447BIB001","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.4310\/JSG.2012.v10.n1.a3"},{"key":"S0129167X24500447BIB003","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.4310\/JSG.2021.v19.n4.a1"},{"key":"S0129167X24500447BIB004","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1112\/topo.12289"},{"key":"S0129167X24500447BIB005","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.4310\/JSG.2022.v20.n3.a1"},{"key":"S0129167X24500447BIB006","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.4310\/JSG.2021.v19.n4.a2"},{"key":"S0129167X24500447BIB007","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2140\/gt.2012.16.301"},{"key":"S0129167X24500447BIB008","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2140\/agt.2016.16.971"},{"issue":"1","key":"S0129167X24500447BIB009","first-page":"1","volume":"57","author":"Chantraine B.","year":"2024","journal-title":"Ann. Sci. \u00c9c. Norm. Sup\u00e9r. (4)"},{"key":"S0129167X24500447BIB010","doi-a